# Run artifacts are large, machine-specific and reproducible from the tools. 701 MB of them, and
# 846 JSON files. They are evidence for a verdict, not source: drop the contents.
*
!.gitignore

# EXCEPT the two kinds that are neither large nor reproducible.
#
# 1. The written reports. A verdict cites `reports/<piece>-survey.md` as its evidence, and until
#    now that path was unversioned — so an agent that overwrote one had destroyed the thing a
#    verdict rests on with no history to recover it from. That happened: the W1-05 builder
#    overwrote its own journey artifact, restored what it could exactly, and had to flag two
#    fields it could not recover rather than invent them. 106 files, 800 KB.
# 2. The blog feed. It is the owner's view of progress and it is append-only by convention, which
#    is exactly the file a careless `>` destroys.
# git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so descend first, then pick.
!*/
!**/*.md
!blog-feed.jsonl

# Still ignored, deliberately: reports/runs/ raw logs (tools/run.mjs writes there by design),
# every .json artifact, and every capture. Those are reproducible by re-running the tool that
# made them, which is the test for whether something belongs in history.
reports/runs/
